# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_py_test_shadow_resolve.py" "PY TEST-SHADOW RESOLVE GATE: PASS" "python test-fixture shadow resolution (precision, recall-safe)" "python test-fixture shadow resolution: a Python test tree (tests/units/...) frequently MIRRORS the package directory layout, so a dotted import of a package module (from reflex_base.utils import types -> suffix reflex_base/utils) suffix-matches BOTH the real package file AND a test-fixture that shadows the same path (tests/units/reflex_base/utils/__init__.py) -- the recall-biased suffix probe fanned out to the test mirror, minting a FALSE production->test coupling (real-repo audit on reflex-dev/reflex: 158 such edges, 6 surviving hub-dampening to a customer warn -- the SAME class the Go _test.go / C# _CS_TEST_SEG / Rust separate-compile-target resolvers already guard, which the Python dotted-suffix probe lacked). FIX (mirrors tests/audit_repo.py src_to_test_real): when a Python import co-resolves to BOTH a test-path file AND a NON-test file, the non-test file is the module the import names and the test-path candidate is the fixture-mirror false edge -> drop it, ONLY in that case. RECALL-SAFE: a real from tests.foo import x (the import literally names a test path -> no non-test sibling co-resolves) is KEPT, and a genuine module under an examples/ package (a unique suffix -> no non-test sibling) is KEPT -- the guard fires only when a non-test sibling PROVES the test candidate is the shadow, never alone. CONTENT-FREE: only file paths and the dotted module name cross, never a file body. Inert on non-Python layouts (the guard is .py-only) and on a flat python app with no test tree. Deterministic synthetic fixtures through the real extractor, no DB" "python test-fixture shadow: a dotted package import that suffix-matches BOTH the real package file and a tests/ mirror drops the test-fixture shadow (false production->test edge) while keeping the real package edge; recall-safe (a genuine from-tests import and a unique examples/ module both survive), content-free, .py-only" 20
